---

<ServiceLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="UX/UI design for websites, stores and apps | SEZMOO"
  description="We design UX/UI for websites, online stores, apps and digital products – user journeys, information architecture, prototypes and a design system ready for development."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<div class="sd">
<section class="sd__hero shell">
  <span class="sd__kick reveal"><i></i>Services</span>
  <h1 class="sd__h1 reveal">UX/UI <span style="color:#ffd200">design.</span></h1>
  <p class="sd__lead reveal" data-d="1"><b>An interface should guide the user</b>, not make them guess.</p>
  <p class="sd__lead reveal" data-d="1">We design websites, online stores, apps and digital products – from user journeys and information architecture, through prototypes, to a design system ready for development.</p>
  <div class="sd__facts reveal" data-d="2">
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Scope</span><strong>Web · store · apps</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Design</span><strong>UX · UI · prototype</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Tools</span><strong>Figma · Adobe CC</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Output</span><strong>Design system and prototype</strong></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="sd__reel reveal" style="background:transparent;border:0" data-d="1">
    <img src="/assets/optimized/lcp/ux-ui-soho-form-868c5c24-1920.webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/lcp/ux-ui-soho-form-868c5c24-800.webp 800w, /assets/optimized/lcp/ux-ui-soho-form-868c5c24-1280.webp 1280w, /assets/optimized/lcp/ux-ui-soho-form-868c5c24-1920.webp 1920w" sizes="100vw" width="1920" height="1080" alt="Soho Form – website design" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" style="object-fit:contain" />
    <figcaption><b>Soho Form</b><span>Website design</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<div class="sd__body shell">
  <div>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-overview">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>Overview</span></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <h3 class="fmt-lead reveal">Good design is not pretty screens – it is the right decisions.</h3>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">What the user sees first, where they click and what they do next decides whether a site sells or just looks nice. That is why we start with the business goal and the people who will actually use the product.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">From there we build the structure, wireframes and a visual layer consistent with the brand. Every project is tested on a clickable prototype before it reaches developers – so a change costs hours, not weeks of rework.</p>
      <div class="sd__more reveal"><a class="is-lead" href="#ux-research">Research ↓</a><a href="#architecture">Architecture ↓</a><a href="#ui-design">UI design ↓</a><a href="#prototypes">Prototypes ↓</a><a href="#design-system">Design system ↓</a></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="ux-research">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>01</span><h2>UX research &amp; workshops</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We start by talking through goals, audiences and constraints. We look at competitors, the data available and the paths users take today to reach their goal – or where they get lost.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">The result is a shared picture of what the product should do and for whom, before the first screen is drawn.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Discovery workshops</span><span>Competitor analysis</span><span>Personas</span><span>User journeys</span><span>UX audit</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="architecture">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>02</span><h2>Information architecture &amp; wireframes</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We organise content and features into a structure that makes sense to the user, not to the company org chart.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">Wireframes show the layout of key views without colour or imagery, which keeps the conversation on what matters: the order of information and the path to contact.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Sitemap</span><span>Information architecture</span><span>Wireframes</span><span>User scenarios</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="ui-design">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>03</span><h2>UI design</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We give the interface the character of the brand. Typography, colour, icons and components are designed view by view – for desktop and mobile.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">Photo, video and graphics are produced by the same team, so the design never waits on material and looks consistent from day one.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>UI design</span><span>Responsive design</span><span>Mobile first</span><span>Micro-interactions</span><span>Interface motion</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="prototypes">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>04</span><h2>Prototypes &amp; testing</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">A clickable prototype lets you move through the product as if it were already live. We use it to test navigation, forms and key flows – with the client team and with users.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">Findings go back into the design before a single line of code is written.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Clickable prototype</span><span>User testing</span><span>A/B testing</span><span>Accessibility (WCAG)</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="design-system">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>05</span><h2>Design system &amp; handover</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We finish with an organised set of components, styles and rules. Developers build it 1:1, and the client team can grow the product without the look drifting.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We can build it in-house too – as part of our <a href="/en/services/websites-and-landing-pages/" style="color:var(--fg);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#ffd200;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px">Websites</a> service.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Component library</span><span>Styles and tokens</span><span>Developer specs</span><span>Build supervision</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-proces">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>How we work</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="sd__steps">
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Workshop</h3><p>Goal, audience and scope – what the product needs to do.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Architecture</h3><p>Content structure and wireframes of key views.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>UI design</h3><p>Look and feel, components and mobile versions.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Prototype</h3><p>A clickable version to validate before build.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Handover</h3><p>Design system and files ready for development.</p></div>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-work">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>Selected work</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="sd__work">
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/en/realizacja-primespot/"><div class="sd__wm"><img src="/assets/portfolio/primespot/pjur-blue-wide-2.jpg" alt="PrimeSpot – Landing · Campaign" loading="lazy" /></div><span>Landing · Campaign</span><h3>PrimeSpot ↗</h3></a>
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/realizacja-world-of-warships/"><div class="sd__wm"><img src="/assets/work/captains-club-int.avif" alt="World of Warships – Event · Digital" loading="lazy" /></div><span>Event · Digital</span><h3>World of Warships ↗</h3></a>
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/en/realizacja-soho-form/"><div class="sd__wm"><img src="/assets/portfolio/soho-form/soho-mockup.webp" alt="Soho Form – UX/UI · Website" loading="lazy" /></div><span>UX/UI · Website</span><h3>Soho Form ↗</h3></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sd__more reveal">
        <a class="is-lead" href="/en/portfolio-en/#pt-grid">Full portfolio ↗</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=video#pt-grid">Video</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=animacje#pt-grid">Animation</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=eventy#pt-grid">Events</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=grafika#pt-grid">Graphics</a>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-faq">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>FAQ – common questions</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <details class="sd__g reveal" open><summary><h3>What is the difference between UX and UI?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>UX is the logic of the product: structure, flows and how easily people reach their goal. UI is the layer you see – typography, colour and components. We design both, because one does not work without the other.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>I already have a website. Can it be improved without starting over?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Yes. We start with a UX audit, show where users get lost and design changes in order of impact.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>Which tools do you use?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Figma and the full Adobe Creative Cloud suite – we pick the tool for the task, not the other way round. You get access to the files, the prototype and the design system, with no locked formats.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>Will you build the site you designed?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Yes. Development is done in-house – from WordPress, through React, to any technology the project needs. See our <a href="/en/services/websites-and-landing-pages/" style="color:var(--fg);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#ffd200;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px">Websites</a> service.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>How long does a UX/UI project take?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>It depends on scope – a landing page is a different scale from a store or an app. We give a timeline and a quote after the brief or a short workshop.</p></div></details>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-related">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>See also</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="svcA" style="margin-top:0">
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/websites-and-landing-pages/"><span class="svcA__no">01</span><h3 class="svcA__t">Websites</h3><p class="svcA__d">Development in WordPress, React or any other stack.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/graphic-design/"><span class="svcA__no">02</span><h3 class="svcA__t">Graphic design</h3><p class="svcA__d">Logos, key visuals and advertising material.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/visual-identity/"><span class="svcA__no">03</span><h3 class="svcA__t">Visual identity</h3><p class="svcA__d">The brand system the interface is built on.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sub-cta reveal">
        <div><h2>Let’s talk about your project.</h2><p>Tell us what you want to build and for whom. We will come back with a proposed scope and timeline.</p></div>
        <a href="/en/#kontakt" class="btn btn--primary"><span class="ico"></span><span class="lbl">Get in touch</span></a>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</ServiceLayout>
